WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.757
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:06.057 --> 00:00:09.338
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.638 --> 00:00:16.145
Unit twenty-one: The Mekong Region. Today you will set conditions with unless, provided that and as long as.

4
00:00:16.445 --> 00:00:18.889
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:23.043
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:24.838
Mekong.

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.090
Mekong means the great river that flows through six Southeast Asian countries.

8
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:32.776
The Mekong feeds millions of people.

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:35.792
Your turn. Say: Mekong.

10
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:39.762
Mekong.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.355
River.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.812
River means a large natural stream of water flowing to the sea.

13
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:48.788
The river floods every rainy season.

14
00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:52.256
Your turn. Say: River.

15
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:55.892
River.

16
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.442
Dam.

17
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.738
Dam means a wall built across a river to hold back water.

18
00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.408
The dam produces electricity.

19
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:07.263
Your turn. Say: Dam.

20
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:10.892
Dam.

21
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.674
Fisheries.

22
00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:17.424
Fisheries means places or industries where fish are caught and sold.

23
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:20.399
Fisheries provide protein for the region.

24
00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:23.647
Your turn. Say: Fisheries.

25
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.466
Fisheries.

26
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.229
Upstream.

27
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:33.876
Upstream means towards the source of a river, against the flow.

28
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:36.262
The dam was built upstream.

29
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.781
Your turn. Say: Upstream.

30
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:43.588
Upstream.

31
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:45.281
Downstream.

32
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:49.757
Downstream means in the direction the river flows, towards its mouth.

33
00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.396
Farmers downstream lost water.

34
00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:55.299
Your turn. Say: Downstream.

35
00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.378
Downstream.

36
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:01.327
Cooperation.

37
00:02:02.317 --> 00:02:06.069
Cooperation means countries working together to reach a shared aim.

38
00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:09.043
Cooperation protects shared water.

39
00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.418
Your turn. Say: Cooperation.

40
00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.477
Cooperation.

41
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:18.427
Livelihoods.

42
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:23.378
Livelihoods means the ways in which people earn money and food to live.

43
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:26.273
Livelihoods depend on a healthy river.

44
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:29.733
Your turn. Say: Livelihoods.

45
00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:33.939
Livelihoods.

46
00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:38.117
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:45.711
Visal, an engineer says 'Fish stocks will survive provided that the dam releases enough water.' What does 'provided that' mean?

48
00:02:46.817 --> 00:02:59.282
It means 'only if'. Provided that, providing, as long as and on condition that all set a condition. They use the present tense for the future: provided that the dam releases water.

49
00:03:00.383 --> 00:03:01.884
What about 'unless'?

50
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:13.684
'Unless' means 'if not'. 'Fisheries will collapse unless the flow is protected' equals 'if the flow is not protected'. Do not add a second negative after unless.

51
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:16.191
Why is it useful?

52
00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:31.755
It states clear conditions in agreements and reports: 'Upstream countries may build dams as long as they inform downstream neighbours.' It makes cooperation rules precise.

53
00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.516
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:39.730
Grammar focus: Conditions: unless and provided that and as long as.

55
00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.344
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:45.141
Fisheries will collapse unless the river flow is protected.

57
00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:49.547
Fish stocks will survive provided that the dam releases enough water.

58
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.272
Upstream countries may build dams as long as they inform their neighbours.

59
00:03:55.233 --> 00:04:03.635
Unless = if not (never add another not). Provided that / as long as / on condition that = only if. Use the present tense, not will, in the condition.

60
00:04:04.383 --> 00:04:08.382
Be careful! Don't say: We will go unless it will rain.

61
00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:12.716
Say: We will go unless it rains.

62
00:04:13.016 --> 00:04:15.155
Use the present tense after unless.

63
00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:18.723
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:19.533 --> 00:04:21.243
Sharing the Mighty Mekong.

65
00:04:21.543 --> 00:04:26.770
The Mekong River flows through six countries and supports the livelihoods of tens of millions of people.

66
00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:32.878
A dam upstream can produce electricity, but it may reduce fish for communities downstream.

67
00:04:33.867 --> 00:04:37.910
Fisheries will decline unless water and sediment continue to flow naturally.

68
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:44.185
Cooperation is possible provided that countries share data and warn each other about water releases.

69
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:50.218
Agreements can work as long as every country accepts that the river belongs to the whole region.

70
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:55.440
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:56.283 --> 00:04:58.503
The crops will die blank it rains soon.

72
00:04:58.803 --> 00:05:02.469
A, unless. B, if. C, provided that.

73
00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.010
The answer is A: unless.

74
00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.626
We will sign blank they accept the conditions.

75
00:05:11.926 --> 00:05:15.509
A, unless. B, provided that. C, although.

76
00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.275
The answer is B: provided that.

77
00:05:22.417 --> 00:05:24.126
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:05:24.426 --> 00:05:33.478
A, Unless the dam doesn't open, fish will die.. B, Unless the dam opens, fish will die.. C, Unless the dam will open, fish die..

79
00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:40.461
The answer is B: Unless the dam opens, fish will die..

80
00:05:41.617 --> 00:05:44.057
The direction towards the river's mouth is blank.

81
00:05:44.357 --> 00:05:47.964
A, upstream. B, downstream. C, inland.

82
00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.511
The answer is B: downstream.

83
00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:58.461
According to the reading, how many countries does the Mekong flow through?

84
00:05:58.761 --> 00:06:01.752
A, three. B, six. C, nine.

85
00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.288
The answer is B: six.

86
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.605
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:15.123
Why does a dam in one country matter to another?

88
00:06:23.917 --> 00:06:25.301
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:49.261
A dam changes the flow, timing and quality of water for everyone downstream. Upstream dams can trap sediment and block fish, which reduces fisheries and farmland in other countries. Because the Mekong crosses many borders, countries need to share information and agree on rules. Cooperation protects livelihoods and prevents disputes over water.

90
00:06:49.561 --> 00:06:51.410
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:52.317 --> 00:06:58.185
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conditions: unless and provided that and as long as.

92
00:06:58.485 --> 00:07:04.864
Today's value is environmental responsibility. Small green actions at home help the whole planet.

93
00:07:05.164 --> 00:07:07.793
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:11.419
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

